// COMMAND CENTRE — the base HQ, and a building you WALK INTO.
//
// The collider is no longer one box around the whole shed (which is what made
// every facility a solid block you bounced off). It is a SHELL: the model's own
// geometry, voxelised and merged into as few axis-aligned boxes as possible, so
// walls are walls, the roof is a roof, and the openings the mesh actually has
// stay open. You enter through the covered span between the two halves and turn
// into either room.
//
// The scale is 6.0. The floor was 4.2, set by the doorway: at 3.0 the way in
// was clear to 1.6 m and the astronaut is a 2.0 m capsule, and a doorway you
// cannot fit through is a wall with a picture of a door on it. 6.0 is the
// HEADQUARTERS reading — the building reads as the thing the whole base is
// arranged around instead of a shed you could miss from thirty metres, and the
// opening clears 3.1 m with it. Check the opening after any change with:
//
//     python3 solar/tools/shell_collider.py models/space-kit/hangar_largeA.glb \
//         --scale 6.0 --check
//
// The boxes below do NOT need regenerating for a scale change — they are in
// CENTRED MODEL units, so the node scale applies to them exactly as it does to
// the mesh. Regenerate (no --check) only if the MODEL changes.
//
// Generated shell: 24 boxes, voxel cell 0.136 model units
// (2.00 x 1.00 x 3.00 model → 12.0 x 6.0 x 18.0 world; seat 3.000).
